        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "243c04a3-452e-5902-b66b-9a1a5076d2bb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: The Justice Collective\n- People: Jon Morter, The Morters\n- Events: Hillsborough disaster\n- Places: Hillsborough football stadium, Sheffield, England, Leppings Lane stand\n- Topics: fund-raising records, charity singles\n\nFacts:\n- On 15 April 1989, the Hillsborough disaster was a human crush at Hillsborough football stadium in Sheffield, England, during the 1988–89 FA Cup semi-final between Liverpool and Nottingham Forest.\n- The Hillsborough disaster crush occurred in the two standing-only central pens in the Leppings Lane stand that were allocated to Liverpool supporters.\n- In 2012, The Justice Collective was originally established as a fund-raising record to raise money for charities associated with the Hillsborough disaster.\n- The Justice Collective is a collective of musicians and celebrities.\n- Jon Morter and the Morters supported alternative singles by Rick Astley in 2008, Rage Against the Machine in 2009, Nirvana in 2011, and The Justice Collective in 2012.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "87c7b428-1000-5e6a-9939-373e166830be",
        "text": "Page: The Justice Collective. Sentence: The Justice Collective is a collective of musicians and celebrities.\nPage: The Justice Collective. Sentence: It was originally established in 2012 as a fund-raising record raising money for the various charities associated with the Hillsborough disaster.\nPage: Hillsborough disaster. Sentence: The Hillsborough disaster was a human crush at Hillsborough football stadium in Sheffield, England on 15 April 1989, during the 1988–89 FA Cup semi-final game between Liverpool and Nottingham Forest.\nPage: Hillsborough disaster. Sentence: The crush occurred in the two standing-only central pens in the Leppings Lane stand, allocated to Liverpool supporters.\nPage: Jon Morter. Sentence: The Morters have supported alternative singles by Rick Astley (2008), Rage Against the Machine (2009), Nirvana (2011), and The Justice Collective (2012).",
